cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article that introduced the method
  (given below as the preferred citation) and state the version of genesis-gwas used.
title: "genesis-gwas: GENetic Effect-Size distribution Inference from Summary-level data"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation, for CPUs and GPUs, of the GENESIS method for estimating the
  effect-size distribution of common variants from GWAS summary statistics and an LD
  reference panel, and for projecting the yield of future studies. It is a
  re-implementation of the GENESIS R package by Yan Zhang, Guanghao Qi, Ju-Hyun Park
  and Nilanjan Chatterjee.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jeya Balaji
    family-names: Balasubramanian
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeyabbalas/GENESIS"
url: "https://jeyabbalas.github.io/GENESIS/"
keywords:
  - GWAS
  - summary statistics
  - effect-size distribution
  - polygenicity
  - heritability
  - composite likelihood
  - statistical genetics
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Estimation of complex effect-size distributions using summary-level statistics
    from genome-wide association studies across 32 complex traits
  authors:
    - given-names: Yan
      family-names: Zhang
    - given-names: Guanghao
      family-names: Qi
    - given-names: Ju-Hyun
      family-names: Park
    - given-names: Nilanjan
      family-names: Chatterjee
  journal: Nature Genetics
  volume: 50
  issue: 9
  start: 1318
  end: 1326
  year: 2018
  doi: 10.1038/s41588-018-0193-x
references:
